# AIRoute UI & CSS reuse rules

1. Global CSS safety
   - Never modify `src/app/globals.css` unless the user explicitly asks for a global style change.
   - Prefer local styles via Tailwind classes inside each component.
   - Do NOT reset base fonts, body margins, or global background colors without confirmation.

2. Reuse shared UI components
   - When implementing or updating any page UI, always reuse existing components from `src/components` instead of re-creating similar styles.
   - Prefer these components:
     - Layout: `PageShell`, `PageHeader` from `src/components/layout`.
     - Basic UI: `Button`, `Badge`, `Chip` from `src/components/ui`.
     - Search: `ToolSearchBar`, `ToolFilterChips` from `src/components/search`.
     - Tools: `ToolCard`, `ToolGrid` from `src/components/tools`.
   - If you need a new variation, extend the existing component with props (e.g. `variant`, `size`) instead of cloning the same JSX in a new file.

3. UI Lab page
   - `/ui-lab` is the internal playground for components.
   - When adding or changing shared UI components, update `/ui-lab` as well so we can visually check them.
   - Do NOT link `/ui-lab` from the public navigation.

4. Language
   - All code comments, component names, and file names should stay in English.
   - Explanations and summaries for the user should be written in Korean.
